      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="best-for"><strong>Best for:</strong> Agencies and in-house content teams who want AEO data integrated into their existing editorial workflow, not as a standalone dashboard.</div>
</div>

<div class="tool-card">
  <h3>Goodie</h3>
  <p class="tagline">Lightweight AEO monitoring focused on tracking visibility over time.</p>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="pros">
      <h4>Strengths</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Simple, focused UX — does one thing well</li>
        <li>Affordable monthly entry point</li>
        <li>Clean trend visualisations</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="cons">
      <h4>Weaknesses</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Measurement only — no action plan or recommendations</li>
        <li>No Claude or Gemini coverage</li>
        <li>Limited drill-down on per-query findings</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="best-for"><strong>Best for:</strong> Solo founders or small teams who want a number to watch monthly and will write their own action plan from the data.</div>
</div>

<h2>What's structurally missing across all of them</h2>

<div class="gap-box">
  <h3>1. Native AI Mode (?udm=50) measurement</h3>
  <p>Most tools that claim Google AI coverage are measuring AI Overview, not AI Mode. AI Mode has a different ranking pipeline and renders on 100% of queries vs AIO's 25–48%. We're aware of only a handful of tools (including monitoraeo) that measure AI Mode separately. Expect this to become standard in 2026.</p>
</div>

<div class="gap-box">
  <h3>2. Public benchmark data</h3>
  <p>No AEO tool other than monitoraeo publishes per-industry AEO rankings as crawlable Dataset pages. Most keep all their data private behind login. This is a strategic miss — published benchmarks earn backlinks AND make the tool itself more cite-worthy by AI engines.</p>
</div>

<div class="gap-box">
  <h3>3. Content workflow integrations</h3>
  <p>SEO tools (Surfer, Frase, Clearscope) integrate with Notion, Webflow, WordPress, Google Docs. AEO tools mostly don't yet. Athena is closest but the integrations are still shallow. Expect rapid evolution here — whoever ships Surfer-for-AEO first will own the content-team buyer.</p>
</div>

<h2>How to pick</h2>
<p>Practical decision tree:</p>

<ul class="bullets">
  <li><strong>Want a single $29 diagnostic to see where you stand?</strong> → monitoraeo Two Engine Audit</li>
  <li><strong>Want full 5-engine coverage with action plan, one-off?</strong> → monitoraeo Full Audit ($79)</li>
  <li><strong>Want monthly tracking on a budget?</strong> → monitoraeo Two Engine Monitoring ($35/mo) or Goodie</li>
  <li><strong>Want monthly tracking across all engines?</strong> → monitoraeo Full Monitoring ($95/mo) or Peec AI</li>
  <li><strong>Have $1k/mo budget and enterprise needs?</strong> → Profound</li>
  <li><strong>Are an agency managing content for multiple clients?</strong> → Athena + standalone measurement tool</li>
  <li><strong>Already use ChatGPT + Perplexity heavily, don't need Claude/Gemini?</strong> → Otterly.ai</li>
</ul>

<h2>Try the cheapest path first</h2>
<p>The honest advice: run monitoraeo's free preview before paying anyone. It takes 30 seconds, costs nothing, and shows you whether your brand is named or cited in Google AI Overviews. If you're already visible there, you may not need full AEO tooling yet. If you're invisible, you'll know exactly where to focus.</p>

